Kept the query string of a client's redirect URI when the authorization endpoint answers. A client registered with a redirect URI such as `https://stats.example.org/index.php?module=RebelOIDC&action=callback&provider=oidc` was sent back to `…&provider=oidc?code=…`, so it never found the `code`, and a refusal's `error` was lost the same way. The response parameters are now added to the registered query, as RFC 6749 requires. @ericof
